<p>London police arrested 523 people at a demonstration in Trafalgar Square on April 11 in support of Palestine Action, a pro-Palestinian group Britain had banned. Protesters held placards backing the group and staged a sit-down rally. Police said that by showing support for a banned organization, participants made themselves liable to arrest. The protest was the first since London’s High Court ruled in February that the designation of Palestine Action as a terrorist organization was unlawful. The British government has since won permission for Interior Minister Shabana Mahmood to appeal that ruling, leaving the ban’s legal status at the center of a wider dispute over public order and protest rights.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/lpy13aK53AHyLgQRQIvkIsEUQLtDiZck3K_8xHEBq2Q5W05-FTMaAL9wSo5sZQbRFn0B7yMXol0zniETJAHwiLL1OcVLu9RAt9UKwBgHnLyli_A7sOCD-L5PmKN9KsITCx5zTb92QD82St5owOTZd2V0M9VYKu58FuI8LB-Os9h-pJs' alt='A man is escorted away by police as protesters gather to call for the lifting of the ban on the Palestine Action group during a demonstration in Trafalgar Square in central London on April 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Arrest revisions: Early reports put the total at more than 200 or 212, but later coverage said police had arrested 523 people, showing the count rose sharply as processing continued.</li><li>Police tactics: Officers carried activists away from the sit-down demonstration while other protesters cheered and clapped in Trafalgar Square.</li><li>Ban trigger: Straits Times reported that lawmakers banned Palestine Action in 2025 after members of the group broke into a Royal Air Force base.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Metropolitan Police: Police said protesters became liable to arrest by displaying placards supporting a banned organization during the Trafalgar Square demonstration. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/london-police-arrest-200-protest-backing-banned-group-131953878'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>High Court: The court ruled in February that the ban on Palestine Action as a terrorist organization was unlawful. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/london-police-arrest-212-people-protest-over-palestine-action-ban'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>British government: Interior Minister Shabana Mahmood won approval to appeal the High Court ruling. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/london-police-arrest-212-people-protest-over-palestine-action-ban'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/london-police-arrest-212-people-at-protest-over-palestine-action-ban'>London police arrest 523 people at protest over Palestine Action ban</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/london-police-arrest-200-protest-backing-banned-group-131953878'>London police arrest more than 200 at protest backing banned group Palestine Action</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/london-police-arrest-212-people-protest-over-palestine-action-ban'>London police arrest 212 people at protest over Palestine Action ban</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/over-500-arrested-at-pro-palestine-rally-in-london-11345372#publisher=newsstand'>Over 500 Arrested At Pro-Palestine Rally In London</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/12/over-500-arrested-at-london-rally-in-support-of-the-banned-group-palestine-action_6752328_4.html'>Over 500 arrested at London rally in support of the banned group Palestine Action</a> - lemonde.fr</li></ul>